  "title": "India and UK Sign New Free Trade Agreement to Secure 642 Cars",
  "summary": "India and the UK have agreed to a free trade agreement to secure 642 vehicles under a bilateral trade quota, with the UK's seven companies seeking applications for this. The agreement aims to boost trade and cooperation between the two countries.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "India and the UK have agreed to a free trade agreement to secure 642 vehicles under a bilateral trade quota.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The UK's seven companies sought applications for the import of 642 vehicles under the agreement.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The quota for these vehicles is set under the India-UK Comprehensive Economic and Trade Agreement (CETA).",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
