    {
      "title": "India gets applications for just 642 UK cars under 10,000-unit FTA quota",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/industry/news/india-gets-applications-for-just-642-uk-cars-under-10-000-unit-fta-quota-126091601162_1.html",
      "description": "Seven UK-based carmakers sought concessional-duty quotas for 642 vehicles after India invited applications for 10,480 units under the bilateral trade agreement for 2026",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-16T14:32:53"
    },
    {
      "title": "DGFT go-ahead for 7 firms to import 642 cars from UK under free trade pact",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/industry/auto/dgft-go-ahead-for-7-firms-to-import-642-cars-from-uk-under-free-trade-pact-126091600636_1.html",
      "description": "The commerce ministry's arm DGFT has approved applications of seven companies for the import of 642 cars for the remainder of this year from Britain under the tariff rate quota provisions of the India-UK free trade agreement, an official said on Wednesday.\nThe Directorate General of Foreign Trade (DGFT) in July invited applications for the allocation of 2026 import quotas for fully-built passenger cars and goods vehicles under the duty concession provisions of the agreement. The applications were sought for a quota for about 5,000 units.\n\"The directorate had received applications from eight companies. We have approved applications of seven. Quota has been approved for 642 cars,\" the official said.\nUnder the India-UK Comprehensive Economic and Trade Agreement (CETA), which came into effect on July 15, New Delhi has allowed the import of a total of 3.78 lakh units of conventional-engine passenger cars, including those in the mass segment, from the UK at a concessional customs duty ...",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-16T09:50:40"
    }
  ]
